===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A person in whom one can [[confide]] or share one's secrets: a friend.
#: {{hyponyms|en|confidante}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1675|author=w:John Dryden|title=Aureng-zebe|publisher=William Miller|year_published=1808|section=page [https://books.google.com/books?id=KPoOAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA223&lpg=PA223&dq=you+love+me+for+no+other+end+than+to+become+my+confidant+and+friend+dryden&source=bl&ots=9C7--Vk9MH&sig=ijsttJA3UdsCaoh1PnEo3Q2I1H0&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwj04KfA99DJAhUE2GMKHZrHBEwQ6AEIMDAG#v=onepage&q&f=false 223]
|passage=Heaven made you love me for no other end, / But to become my '''confidant''' and friend: / As such, I keep no secret from your sight, […]}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Kenneth Graham|title=w:The Golden Age|location=London|year=1895|page=5|passage=One in thought and purpose, linked by the necessity of combating one hostile fate, a power antagonistic ever, - a power we lived to evade, - we had no '''confidants''' save ourselves.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en-GB|author=Victoria Bekiempis|title=‘Dark’ donations, free love and the fall: the Sam Bankman-Fried trial is here|work=The Guardian|date=2023-09-30|url=https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/sep/30/what-is-sam-bankman-fried-trial-for-new-york-ftx-crypto|issn=0261-3077|passage=Bankman-Fried’s '''confidants''' were along for the ride. At his side was Caroline Ellison, Alameda’s CEO and his on-again, off-again lover.}}

